02-1_21","eisbn":["9783658393021"],"isbn":["9783658393014"],"publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Pflegeinnovationen in der Praxis"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-43c65b43-a662-44f7-9fed-c6c46e93282e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Forschungs- und Entwicklungsprojekte in der Pflege erfolgreich planen und umsetzen – Voraussetzungen und Gelingensbedingungen am Beispiel des Einsatzes von künstlicher Intelligenz","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695238","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This minitrack provides a venue for all work (qualitative, quantitative, computational, and design) in relation to better understanding health data platforms, data repositories, data sharing, data governance, and ecosystems. It highlights various perspectives, including technical, organizational, social, and regulatory ones and considers multiple levels, such as the system, individual, community, and societal level. This minitrack encourages work on emergent technologies, while it is open to learn how existing technologies may be repurposed for data-driven care coordination and research using increasing amounts of data over long periods of time.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fürstenau, Daniel","Witte, Anne-Katrin","Thiebes, Scott","Sunyaev, Ali"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695285"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","University of Hagen"],"keyword":["Data sharing","Ecosystems","Health data","Openness","Platforms","Privacy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction to the minitrack on data platforms and ecosystems in healthcare","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101716508/m-intro-0069.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695285","ids":["itu-b986aa70-1413-4f2f-9942-8785757c0391"],"keyword":["Data sharing","Ecosystems","Health data","Openness","Platforms","Privacy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-27BF09F0AC54682DAB38B25D1C93FD09"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101716508/m-intro-0069.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of hagen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hagen","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"karlsruhe institute of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"fürstenaupau","last":"Fürstenau","locid":"ceef6d97-26fe-4163-9538-6685e98bce2e","name":"Fürstenau, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-8490-7707","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Katrin","key":"wittepau","last":"Witte","name":"Witte, Anne-Katrin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Scott","key":"thiebespau","last":"Thiebes","name":"Thiebes, Scott","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ali","key":"sunyaevpau","last":"Sunyaev","name":"Sunyaev, Ali","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 56th Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b986aa70-1413-4f2f-9942-8785757c0391"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Introduction to the Minitrack on Data Platforms and Ecosystems in Healthcare","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695285","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: The circular economy reshapes the linear “take, make, and dispose” approach and evolves around minimizing waste and recapturing resources in a closed-loop system. The health sector accounts for 4.6% of global greenhouse gas emissions and has, over the decades, been built to rely on single-use devices and deal with high volumes of medical waste. With the increase in the adoption of digital health solutions in the health care industry, leading the industry into a new paradigm of how we provide health care, a focus must be put on the amount of waste that will follow. Digital health solutions will shape health care through the use of technology and lead to improved patient care, but they will also make medical waste more complex to deal with due to the e-waste component. Therefore, a transformation of the health care industry to a circular economy is a crucial cornerstone in decreasing the impact on the environment. Objective: This study aims to address the lack of direction in the current literature on circular business models. It will consider micro, meso, and macro factors that would impact the operational validity of circular models using the digital health solutions ePaper label (medical packaging), smart wearable sensor (health monitoring devices), smart pill box (medication management), and endo-cutter (surgical equipment) as examples. Methods: The study will systematically perform a scoping review through a database and snowball search. We will analyze and classify the studies from a predetermined set of categories and then summarize them into an evidence map. Based on the review, the study will develop a 2D framework for businesses to follow or for future research to take a standpoint from. Results: Preliminarily, the review has analyzed 26 studies in total. The results are close to equally distributed among the micro (8/26, 31%), meso (10/26, 38%), and macro (8/26, 31%) levels. Circular economy studies emphasize several circular practices such as recycling (17/26, 65%), reusing (18/26, 69%), reducing (15/26, 58%), and remanufacturing (8/26, 31%). The value proposition in the examined business model is mostly dominated by stand-alone products (18/26, 69%) compared to product as a service (7/26, 27%), involving stakeholders such as health care professionals or hospitals (20/26, 77%), manufacturers (11/26, 42%), and consumers (9/26, 35%). All studies encompass societal (12/26, 46%), economic (23/26, 88%), and environmental (24/26, 92%) viewpoints. Conclusions: The study argues that each digital health solution would have to be accessed individually to find the optimal business model to follow. This is due to their differing life cycles and complexity. The manufacturer will need a layered value proposition, implementing several business models dependent on their respective product portfolios. The need to incorporate several business models implies an ecosystem perspective that is relevant to consider.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rønn, Camille","Wieland, Andreas","Lehrer, Christiane","Marton, Attila","LaRoche, Jason","Specker, Adrien","Leroy, Pascal","Fürstenau, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-710318"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fürstenau, Daniel"],"country":["Belgium","Netherlands","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Janssen: Pharmaceutical Companies of Johnson and Johnson","Waste of Electrical and Electronical Equipment Forum","World Resources Forum Association"],"keyword":["Business model","Circular economy","Digital","Digital Health Solution","Digital health","Digital health solutions","Digital tool","Healthcare","Life cycle","MedTech device","Monitoring device","Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circular business model for digital health solutions protocol for a scoping review","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/47874","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["CR holds funding for a PhD through the IT University of Copenhagen. We acknowledge the financial support of the European Research Executive Agency under the powers delegated by the European Commission for the Digital Health in Circular Economy (DiCE) project (101060184) [15]."],"id":"S01-000.00-710318","identifier":[{"id":"85180073535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-b214847f-c9cc-4c2b-9404-fa6da5842295"],"keyword":["Business model","Circular economy","Digital","Digital health","Digital health solution","Digital health solutions","Digital tool","Healthcare","Life cycle","MedTech device","Monitoring device","Technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-472B62B62CB9E764101F66CC09244296"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/99751202/roenn_camille_et_al_circular_business_model_for_digital_health_solutions_publishersversion.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/47874","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","