{"abstract":"Background and aim While artificial intelligence (AI) is being adapted for various life domains and applications related to medicine and healthcare, the use of AI in nursing practice is still scarce. The German Ministry for Education and Research funded a study in order to explore needs, application scenarios, requirements, facilitators and barriers for research and development projects in the context of AI in nursing care. Method A sequential explorative mixed methods study including a stakeholder and expert workshop (N = 21), expert interviews (N = 14), an online survey (N = 53) and a Datathon (N = 80) was conducted with an emphasis on qualitative data. Results Needs and application scenarios encompassed the micro- and meso-level of care and derived from typical phenomena inherent to nursing care as well as from skill- and staff mix and consequences arising from staff shortages, from the extend of informal care and an associated need for information and education of informal caregivers and nursing assistants. Requirements for and characteristics of successful research and development projects included regulatory, processual, technological, ethical and legal aspects and supportive eco-systems. Conclusion A key element in the design of research projects remains participatory and demand-driven development that aims to bring AI solutions out of the lab and into practice. However, influencing factors remain that are outside the sphere of influence of individual projects, in particular the creation of resilient legal foundations for data use and the use of AI in practice, standardization of data structures and the establishment of infrastructures for data exchange across institutions and projects.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Seibert, Kathrin","Domhoff, Dominik","Fürstenau, Daniel","Biessmann, Felix","Schulte-Althoff, Matthias","Wolf-Ostermann, Karin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695311"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Berliner Hochschule für Technik","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","University of Bremen"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Digital health","Mixed methods","Needs analysis","Nursing Care"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring needs and challenges for ai in nursing care results of an explorative sequential mixed methods study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s44247-023-00015-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695311","ids":["itu-f5eac502-c1ad-4ef1-be1e-9ed713ab9ef5"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Digital Health","Mixed Methods","Needs analysis","Nursing care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-4EFCCF904F1A39881E8A65FC031BDD00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s44247-023-00015-2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of bremen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bremen","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"berliner hochschule für technik","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Berliner Hochschule für Technik","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"charité universitätsmedizin berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathrin","key":"seibertpau","last":"Seibert","name":"Seibert, Kathrin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dominik","key":"domhoffpau","last":"Domhoff","name":"Domhoff, Dominik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"fürstenaupau","last":"Fürstenau","locid":"ceef6d97-26fe-4163-9538-6685e98bce2e","name":"Fürstenau, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-8490-7707","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Felix","key":"biessmannpau","last":"Biessmann","name":"Biessmann, Felix","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"schultealthoffpau","last":"Schulte-Althoff","name":"Schulte-Althoff, Matthias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"wolfostermannpau","last":"Wolf-Ostermann","name":"Wolf-Ostermann, Karin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s44247-023-00015-2","issn":["2731684X"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Digital Health","paperid":"13","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Digital Health","volume":"2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f5eac502-c1ad-4ef1-be1e-9ed713ab9ef5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring needs and challenges for AI in nursing care – results of an explorative sequential mixed methods study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695311","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background Anemia is highly prevalent in patients before hip joint revision surgery (HJRS) and is associated with an increased complication rate. This paper is the first to investigate costs, real diagnosis-related group (DRG) revenues and case coverage of preoperative anemia in elective HJRS. Methods Medical data, transfusions, costs, and revenues of all patients undergoing HJRS at two campuses of the Charité –Universitätsmedizin Berlin between 2010 and 2017 were used for subgroup analyses and linear regressions. Results Of 1187 patients included 354 (29.8%) showed preoperative anemia. A total of 565 (47.6%) patients were transfused with a clear predominance of anemic patients (72.6% vs. 37.0%, p  Conclusion Preoperative anemia and perioperative transfusions in HJRS are associated with increased treatment costs and a financial undercoverage for healthcare providers and health insurance companies. Concepts for the treatment of preoperative anemia (e.g. patient blood management) could reduce treatment costs in the medium term.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Vorderwülbecke, Gerald","Spies, Claudia","von Heymann, Christian","Kruppa, Jochen","Fürstenau, Daniel","Kaufner, Lutz","Werner, Sven","Höft, Moritz","Balzer, Felix"],"cuid":["S02-088.41-672863"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Balzer, Felix","von Heymann, Christian"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Berlin Institute of Health","Charite - Universitatsmedizin Berlin","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Free University of Berlin","Freie Universität Berlin","Humboldt University of Berlin","Vivantes Klinikum im Friedrichshain"],"keyword":["DRG system","Digital health care","Health economics","Patient blood management","Red blood cells","Revenue","Transfusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"die kosten der präoperativen anämie bei hüftgelenkrevisionsoperationen","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00101-022-01211-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.41-672863","identifier":[{"id":"85146224027","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-600a5e05-fea1-46fc-9d3c-b731156c5f39","itu-1a648be5-0888-4478-aa78-9a93a3ed73dd"],"keyword":["DRG-System","Digital health care","Erlöse","Erythrozyten","Patient blood management","Patient blood managment","Red blood cells","Revenue","Transfusion","health economics"],"lang":"German","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-977BB391717D84F3FB23F0F0A829D9DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s00101-022-01211-x.pdf?pdf=button","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00101-022-01211-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/93942831/vorderwulbecke_et_al_die_kosten_der_praoperativen_anamie_bei_huftgelenkrevisionsoperationen_publishersversion.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102674508/s00101-022-01211-x.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"charite universitatsmedizin berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charite - Universitatsmedizin Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"freie universität berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Freie Universität Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"berlin institute of health","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Berlin Institute of Health","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"charité universitätsmedizin berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"vivantes klinikum im friedrichshain","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Vivantes Klinikum im Friedrichshain","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"free university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Free University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"8","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"9","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerald","key":"vorderwülbeckepau","last":"Vorderwülbecke","name":"Vorderwülbecke, Gerald","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Claudia","key":"spiespau","last":"Spies","name":"Spies, Claudia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"vonheymannpau","last":"von Heymann","name":"von Heymann, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"von Heymann","key":"christianpau","last":"Christian","name":"Christian, von Heymann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4 5 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Jochen","key":"kruppapau","last":"Kruppa","name":"Kruppa, Jochen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4 8 9","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"fürstenaupau","last":"Fürstenau","locid":"e1b78deb-bdff-40e4-935b-f1a97937809c","name":"Fürstenau, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-8490-7707","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lutz","key":"kaufnerpau","last":"Kaufner","name":"Kaufner, Lutz","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Sven","key":"wernerpau","last":"Werner","name":"Werner, Sven","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Moritz","key":"höftpau","last":"Höft","name":"Höft, Moritz","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Felix","key":"balzerpau","last":"Balzer","name":"Balzer, Felix","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00101-022-01211-x","issn":["27316858","27316866"],"issn_org":["27316858"],"issue":"1","journal":"Anaesthesiologie","pages":"13-20","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Anaesthesiologie","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146224027"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-600a5e05-fea1-46fc-9d3c-b731156c5f39","itu-1a648be5-0888-4478-aa78-9a93a3ed73dd"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Die Kosten der präoperativen Anämie bei Hüftgelenkrevisionsoperationen","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.41-672863","year":2023,"yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The assumption that generativity engenders unbounded growth has acquired an almost taken-for-granted position in information systems and management literature. Against this premise, we examine the relationship between generativity and user base growth in the context of a digital platform. To do this, we synthesize the literature on generativity into two views, social interaction (expansion of ecosystem boundaries) and product view (expansion of product boundaries), that jointly and individually relate to user base growth. Both views help us explain how opening a platform relates to the emergence and resolution of conflicting expectations in a platform ecosystem that result in new functions and expanded use. We adopt a panel vector autoregressive approach combining data from six large transaction platforms that engaged with open-source developer communities. We found that the dominant narrative of generativity engendering growth, although generally supported by our analysis, obscures the fact that the inverse is also true; that is, growth can lead to expansion of product boundaries (inverse generativity) and that generativity can be bounded; that is, growth can stabilize ecosystem boundaries (bounded generativity). Against this background, we propose an extended generativity theory that presents generativity and growth in an integrative view and raises awareness about the limitations of the “unbounded growth” claim. We conclude that there is value in separating the two views of generativity conceptually and analytically, along with their relationship to user base growth, and we call for research on the pathways through which generativity produces growth.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Fürstenau, Daniel","Baiyere, Abayomi","Schewina, Kai","Schulte-Althoff, Matthias","Rothe, Hannes"],"cuid":["S02-089.29-031915"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fürstenau, Daniel"],"country":["Canada","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charite - Universitatsmedizin Berlin","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Free University of Berlin","Freie Universität Berlin","ICN Business School","Institut commercial de Nancy Business School","Queen's University","University of Duisburg-Essen","Universität Duisburg-Essen"],"keyword":["Digital platforms","Dynamic boundary","Ecosystem boundaries","Generativity","Product boundaries","User base growth"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extended generativity theory on digital platforms","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1287/isre.2023.1209","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.29-031915","identifier":[{"id":"85160426984","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-aa6753c1-49c1-4331-bd01-fef0e9480029","itu-a1ca51aa-da82-45b5-95da-1ab3c6c8537e"],"keyword":["Digital platforms","Dynamic boundary","Ecosystem boundaries","Ecosystems boundaries","Generativity","Product boundaries","User base growth"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4F2C31E6B70AAABF886F1EE00F606DE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1287/isre.2023.1209","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/99364922/daniel_f_rstenau_et_al_extended_generativity_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107005465/ISR_Manuscript_Generativity_preprint.