t Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jane","key":"fedorowiczpedh","last":"Fedorowicz","name":"Fedorowicz, Jane","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Wai Fong","key":"bohpedh","last":"Boh","name":"Boh, Wai Fong","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan Marco","key":"leimeisterpedh","last":"Leimeister","name":"Leimeister, Jan Marco","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sunil","key":"wattalpedh","last":"Wattal","name":"Wattal, Sunil","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9780996683197"],"issn":["00000033"],"place":"Atlanta, GA","publisher":"Association for Information Systems. AIS Electronic Library (AISeL)","series":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 40th International Conference on Information Systems (ICIS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114902189"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-8bd69db7-2d2c-4dfe-b036-edc6f1b05b93"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Growth, Complexity, and Generativity of Digital Platforms : The Case of Otto.de","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-288659","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Digital infrastructures result from individual yet interdependent systems evolving in relation to each other. This paper identifies three processes by which individual systems become embedded into digital infrastructures. The first is a parallel process, whereby systems become embedded independently of each other. The second is a competitive process, whereby systems compete for resources and attention and one system usually thrives while the other system loses importance. The third is a spanning process characterizing a situation of boundary-spanning between distinct parts of a digital infrastructure. The three processes, synthesized into a dynamic model of digital infrastructure embeddedness, offer clarity to the question how digital infrastructures evolve. They also provide insight into the emergence of three forms of digital infrastructures: silofied, regenerated, and unified. Reflecting an interconnection view, our research further facilitates an understanding of infrastructure inertia and its associated consequence. Criticality traps should be avoided by considering the right timing for system replacement in the light of growing embeddedness over time. Digital infrastructures are a result of individual yet interdependent systems evolving in relation to each other. In this paper, we identify three processes by which individual systems become embedded into digital infrastructures. First, there are parallel processes, in which systems become embedded independently of each other. Second, there are competitive processes, in which the embeddedness of one system increases at the expense of another. Finally, there are spanning processes, in which bridges are built between different embedded systems. The three processes, synthesized into a dynamic model of digital infrastructure embeddedness, offer much-needed conceptual clarity to the area of digital infrastructure evolution. They also provide insight into the emergence of three forms of digital infrastructures: silofied, regenerated, and unified. Reflecting an interconnection view, our research further facilitates an understanding of infrastructure inertia and its associated consequence.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fürstenau, Daniel","Baiyere, Abayomi","Kliewer, Natalia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-294237"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Freie Universität Berlin","University of Turku"],"keyword":["Digital infrastructures","Embeddedness","Inertia","Mixed methods","Process models"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a dynamic model of embeddedness in digital infrastructures","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/60814161/abayomi_baiyere_et_al_a_dynamic_model_of_embeddedness_in_digital_infrastructures_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-294237","identifier":[{"id":"85079270774","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-c6064220-fe27-45db-9daa-6be8d0605773"],"keyword":["Digital infrastructures","Embeddedness","Inertia","Mixed methods","Process models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D6B90E3EA13271A6CE00B883ECB5813C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/60814161/abayomi_baiyere_et_al_a_dynamic_model_of_embeddedness_in_digital_infrastructures_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"freie universität berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Freie Universität Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"university of turku","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Turku","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"fürstenaupau","last":"Fürstenau","name":"Fürstenau, Daniel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Abayomi","key":"baiyerepau","last":"Baiyere","locid":"5df73b16-ee57-4a45-a43f-9e6eb629180b","name":"Baiyere, Abayomi","orcid":"0000-0002-2211-4960","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalia","key":"kliewerpau","last":"Kliewer","name":"Kliewer, Natalia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1287/isre.2019.0864","issn":["10477047","15265536"],"issn_org":["10477047"],"issue":"4","journal":"Information Systems Research","pages":"1319-1342","publisher":"Institute for Operations Research and the Management Sciences","status":"p","title":"Information Systems Research","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079270774"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-c6064220-fe27-45db-9daa-6be8d0605773"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"A Dynamic Model of Embeddedness in Digital Infrastructures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-294237","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Purpose – This paper reviews empirical studies on process mining in order to understand its use by organizations. The aim is further to outline future research opportunities. Design/methodology/approach – We propose a classification model that combines core conceptual elements of process mining with prior models from technology classification from the enterprise resource planning (ERP) and business intelligence field. Our model incorporates an organizational usage, a system-orientation and service nature, adding a focus on physical services. Our application is based on a systematic literature review of 144 research papers. Findings – The results show that, thus far, the literature has been chiefly concerned with realization of single business process management systems in single organizations. We conclude that cross-system or cross-organizational process mining is underrepresented in the ISR, as is the analysis of physical services. Practical implications – Process mining researchers have paid little attention to utilising complex use cases and mining mixed physical-digital services. Practitioners should work closely with academics to overcome these knowledge gaps. Only then will process mining be on the cusp of becoming a technology that allows new insights into customer processes by supplying business operations with valuable and detailed information. Originality/value – Despite the scientific interest in process mining, particularly scant attention has been given by researchers to investigating its use in relatively complex scenarios, e.g. cross-system and cross-organizational process mining. Furthermore, coverage on the use of process mining from a service perspective is limited, which fails to reflect the marketing and business context of most contemporary organizations, wherein the importance of such scenarios is widely acknowledged. The small number of studies encountered may be due to a lack of knowledge about the potential of such scenarios as well as successful examples, a situation we seek to remedy with this study.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Thiede, Malte","Fürstenau, Daniel","Barquet, Ana Paula Bezerra"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-279415"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Freie Universität Berlin"],"keyword":["Cyber physical systems","Organizational perspective","Process mining","Service dominant logic","Systematic literature review"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how is process mining technology used by organizations a systematic literature review of empirical studies","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-279415","identifier":[{"id":"000436260100003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85048836629","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-2a88cf9c-5396-4ec1-9426-f8c7184e154f"],"keyword":["Cyber-physical systems","Organizational perspective","Process mining","Service-dominant logic","Systematic literature review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B7F30702ED96C2B55065F682AF69E6EF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"freie universität berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Freie Universität Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malte","key":"thiedepau","last":"Thiede","name":"Thiede, Malte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"fürstenaupau","last":"Fürstenau","locid":"e1b78deb-bdff-40e4-935b-f1a97937809c","name":"Fürstenau, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-8490-7707","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana Paula Bezerra","key":"barquetpau","last":"Barquet","name":"Barquet, Ana Paula Bezerra","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/bpmj-06-2017-0148","issn":["14637154","17584116"],"issn_org":["14637154"],"issue":"4","journal":"Business Process Management Journal","pages":"900-922","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing","status":"p","title":"Business Process Management Journal","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-2a88cf9c-5396-4ec1-9426-f8c7184e154f"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"How Is Process Mining Technology Used by Organizations? : A Systematic Literature Review of Empirical Studies","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-279415","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The simulation of heuristic problems of timetable and rotation planning is a well-established procedure in the local public transport for years. However, agent-based approaches like MATSim have additional potentials, which extend beyond the usual application. This contribution illustrates one of these potentials using the example of the introduction of a service station in the service system of a public transport provider. In a five-step procedure, this service is analyzed and modeled for the simulation. The results of the simulation provide further direction for the specific requirements of these service stations. The case study shows, on the one hand, the usefulness of simulation in a complex service system. Thus, both service station-specific parameters, such as location combinations, capacity or service life, as well as market-economy data, such as utilization, can be calculated. On the other hand, the case also shows the limitations, such as the high computational cost.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thiede, Malte","Stegemann, Lars","Gersch, Martin","Fürstenau, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-283818"],"event":{"end":"2017-02-25","place":"Porto, pt","start":"2017-02-23","title":"International Conference on Operations Research","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Freie Universität Berlin"],"keyword":["Public transport systems","Service simulations","Service systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simulation of a service station in a public transportation system","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-283818","ids":["cbs-582bac70-7bbf-4c26-a7e7-53d70303062a"],"keyword":["Public transport systems","Service simulations","Service systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7B61A2A71D4E392AC0D3CD53B8409DBE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"freie universität berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Freie Universität Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malte","key":"thiedepau","last":"Thiede","name":"Thiede, Malte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"stegemannpau","last":"Stegemann","name":"Stegemann, Lars","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"gerschpau","last":"Gersch","name":"Gersch, Martin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel","key":"fürstenaupau","last":"Fürstenau","locid":"e1b78deb-bdff-40e4-935b-f1a97937809c","name":"Fürstenau, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-8490-7707","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-582bac70-7bbf-4c26-a7e7-53d70303062a"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Simulation of a Service Station in a Public Transportation System","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-283818","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
